## 3. Error taxonomy of the remaining sample errors (deterministic)

{{sample.taxonomy.n_steps}} step differences remain, in three classes:

| Class | Steps | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Unrecoverable | {{sample.taxonomy.unrecoverable}} | the resource appears in no input file or activity; no method can find it |
| Undecidable tie | {{sample.taxonomy.ties}} | several cases fit a worker event equally; `SKIP_MULTI` leaves it unassigned (or the pair order guesses wrong) |
| Tie guess (link extra) | {{sample.taxonomy.tie_guesses}} | a tie-broken assignment gave the case a resource that belongs to another case |
| Other link errors | {{sample.taxonomy.other}} | any miss or extra not explained above |

{{sample.taxonomy.table_md}}

The agent can remove tie guesses but cannot invent evidence for undecidable ties: on the sample it moved precision from {{sample.det.step_p}} to {{sample.agent.step_p}} and recall from {{sample.det.step_r}} to {{sample.agent.step_r}} (cases changed: {{sample.agent_changed_cases}}).

